<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Brooke is an 83-year-old man with right breast cancer, stage IIA and hormone receptor-positive, treated by bilateral mastectomy and right axillary dissection about a year ago, who has taken tamoxifen 20 mg daily for eleven and a half months. He returns for his subsequent annual wellness visit, two months after his survivorship visit, and completed the health risk assessment beforehand. He has missed no tamoxifen doses. Hot flashes are mild and occur two or three times a week; libido is lower but he is not troubled by it. He has had no leg swelling or pain, chest pain, breathlessness, or change in vision. He has no new lump, skin change, or swelling on either side of the chest or in either armpit, and no bone pain, cough, or weight loss. He walks most days and keeps a busy schedule of writing and speaking, including talking to men about breast cancer. He has had no falls, emergency visits, or hospital stays since his operation. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Visit</td><td>Subsequent annual wellness visit</td></tr><tr><td>Safety events</td><td>No falls, emergency visits, or hospital stays since his operation</td></tr><tr><td>Medicines</td><td>Tamoxifen 20 mg daily; cholecalciferol 1000 units daily; no other prescription or over-the-counter medicines</td></tr><tr><td>Active conditions</td><td>Right breast cancer, stage IIA, on adjuvant tamoxifen, no evidence of recurrence; low bone mass at the femoral neck</td></tr><tr><td>Functional status</td><td>Independent in all activities and instrumental activities of daily living</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Health risk assessment. Completed by the patient before the visit and reviewed during the visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Finding</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Self-rated health</td><td>Good</td></tr><tr><td>Psychosocial</td><td>Busy with writing, board work, and speaking; close family and friends; no loneliness or low mood</td></tr><tr><td>Tobacco</td><td>Never used tobacco</td></tr><tr><td>Alcohol and drugs</td><td>Does not drink alcohol (AUDIT-C 0); no other drug use</td></tr><tr><td>Physical activity</td><td>Walks 30 to 40 minutes most days and does light weights twice a week</td></tr><tr><td>Nutrition</td><td>Regular balanced meals; dairy twice a day for calcium</td></tr><tr><td>Sleep</td><td>Seven hours a night; hot flashes wake him about once a week</td></tr><tr><td>Activities of daily living</td><td>Independent</td></tr><tr><td>Instrumental activities of daily living</td><td>Independent; manages his own medicines with a weekly pill organizer; drives</td></tr><tr><td>Home safety</td><td>Smoke detectors working; handrails on the stairs; good lighting</td></tr><tr><td>Falls</td><td>No falls this year; no fear of falling</td></tr><tr><td>Hearing and vision</td><td>No hearing concern; wears reading glasses; eye examination eight months ago</td></tr><tr><td>Memory</td><td>No concerns</td></tr><tr><td>Pain</td><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

