    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.9" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Subsequent annual wellness visit completed</content>. Health risk assessment reviewed and a written prevention plan given. Depression, alcohol, cognitive, and fall-risk screens are negative. Total cholesterol 176, HDL 54, LDL 104 mg/dL. [S]<list><item>Next annual wellness visit in one year.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Right breast cancer, stage IIA, on adjuvant tamoxifen (C50.121)</content>. No symptoms or signs of recurrence about one year after surgery. Surveillance continues by history and examination; no imaging or blood tests are needed without symptoms. [S]<list><item>Survivorship visit in two months, then every three to six months to three years.</item><item>Medical oncology review as scheduled.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Long-term tamoxifen (Z79.810)</content>. Taking it every day with mild hot flashes and a lower libido; no clot symptoms. [S]<list><item>Continue tamoxifen 20 mg daily.</item><item>Keep moving on long journeys and report leg swelling or pain, chest pain, or sudden breathlessness at once.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Personalized prevention plan. A written copy was given to the patient. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Service</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Influenza vaccine, this season</td><td>Completed today</td><td>High-dose vaccine given today</td></tr><tr><td>Pneumococcal vaccine</td><td>Completed today</td><td>PCV20 given today; no earlier pneumococcal vaccine on record; no further doses needed</td></tr><tr><td>Recombinant zoster vaccine</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Dose 1 given today; dose 2 due in two to six months</td></tr><tr><td>RSV vaccine</td><td>Due</td><td>A single dose is recommended at 75 and older; he will get it at the pharmacy with his COVID-19 dose</td></tr><tr><td>COVID-19 vaccine, this season</td><td>Due</td><td>Recommended at his age; at the pharmacy next week</td></tr><tr><td>Tetanus, diphtheria, and pertussis booster</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Tdap eight years ago; next dose due in two years</td></tr><tr><td>Colorectal cancer screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Screening from 76 to 85 is selective; discussed, and not recommended for him now, given his age and his current cancer care</td></tr><tr><td>Prostate cancer screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>PSA screening is not recommended at 70 and older; his germline panel showed no BRCA2 or other variant that would change this</td></tr><tr><td>Breast imaging</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>After bilateral mastectomy there is no breast to image; surveillance is by examination of both sides of the chest wall</td></tr><tr><td>Bone density</td><td>Up to date</td><td>DXA eight months ago: femoral neck T-score -1.2, spine -0.4; vitamin D now 36 ng/mL; repeat in two years</td></tr><tr><td>Cholesterol and statin decision</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Total cholesterol 176, HDL 54, LDL 104 mg/dL; no diabetes or smoking. Risk calculators are not validated beyond 79, and evidence for starting a statin for primary prevention after 75 is limited; not started after discussion; review yearly</td></tr><tr><td>Lung cancer and abdominal aortic aneurysm screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Never used tobacco</td></tr><tr><td>Hepatitis C and HIV screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Outside the recommended age ranges and no risk factors</td></tr><tr><td>Depression screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>PHQ-2 score 0</td></tr><tr><td>Unhealthy alcohol use screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>AUDIT-C score 0</td></tr><tr><td>Cognitive assessment</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Mini-Cog 5 of 5</td></tr><tr><td>Falls prevention</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Timed Up and Go 10 seconds; no falls; walking and light weights continue</td></tr><tr><td>Hearing</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Whispered-voice test passed in both ears</td></tr><tr><td>Eye examination</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Eight months ago; tamoxifen can rarely cause cataract or retinal changes, so he will report any change in vision</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Immunizations given today: High-dose influenza vaccine, 2003-2004 season; Pneumococcal conjugate vaccine PCV20; Recombinant zoster vaccine, dose 1 of 2 [S]</paragraph><paragraph>Guideline basis: CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, breast cancer monograph (2026); Medicare Wellness Visits (Medicare Learning Network) (2026); Medicare Preventive Services reference: visit templates, screening cascades, and documentation elements (2026); USPSTF A and B Recommendations (2026); Adult Immunization Schedule by Age (2026)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Survivorship visit in two months. Second zoster dose in two to six months. COVID-19 and RSV vaccines at the pharmacy. Next annual wellness visit in one year. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
